<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <!--
    PACKAGING IDENTITY IS A CONSUMER CONTRACT AND DOES NOT FOLLOW THE FOLDER.
    This project moved to Plugins/Schema/ during the plugin conversion, but
    Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Schema has shipped tags through v9.4.0: renaming the
    PackageId would break a consumer's PackageReference with no type-forwarding
    possible, and renaming the RootNamespace would break every `using` in their
    code as well. PackageId, RootNamespace and the assembly name (defaulted from
    this file's name) therefore all stay as published. Only genuinely new
    packages - Plugins.Abstractions, DesignSystem - carry a new id.
    The `_content/` static-web-asset path derives from the assembly name, so it
    is _content/Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Schema/ for the same reason.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Schema</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Schema</PackageId>
    <Version>9.4.0</Version>
    <Description>The Schema (enforcement policy, envelope versioning and remediation, compliance, and dead letters) Explorer plugin: a self-contained plugin package carrying its own schema control-API gRPC client, its domain model, its Razor views, and its plugin-scoped stylesheet. Registered with AddExplorerPlugin, gated by its own four-state access gate plus per-tree scoped decisions, and styled against Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.DesignSystem. A head surfaces the area by registering this plugin and withholds it by not registering it; there is no per-area option flag. Served by a referencing app at _content/Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Schema.</Description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/NSTA1/Orleans.Lattice</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/NSTA1/Orleans.Lattice</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageReadmeFile>NUGET_README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="NUGET_README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DynamicProxyGenAssembly2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Unlike Explorer.Core (which is walled off to the state-API client), this
    plugin project is allowed to reference the schema-API (control plane) gRPC
    client, which transitively pulls in the schema model and core. It bridges
    that client to its own domain model, and carries the Razor views and the
    scoped stylesheet that render it, so the shared UI library needs no
    reference to it at all (epic decision D5).

    It takes the design system for the tokens, the breakpoint set, and the
    adaptive primitives, and the plugin abstractions for the contract it
    registers through. Explorer.Core is referenced only for the catalog reader
    its domain adapter projects governable trees from; the views never see Core,
    only ISchemaPluginDomain. It must never reference
    Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.UI: the dependency runs the other way round, from a
    head to a plugin.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Core\Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\DesignSystem\Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.DesignSystem.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Abstractions\Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Plugins.Abstractions.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\lattice.api.schema.grpc\Orleans.Lattice.Api.Schema.Grpc.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Grpc.Net.Client" Version="2.83.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Orleans.Serialization" Version="10.2.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
